{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.138,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "118"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.138,
            0.902,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "**Remark :** Since the hypotenuse is the longest side in a right triangle, the value of sin A or cos A is always less than 1 (or, in particular, equal to 1)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.184,
            0.409,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider some examples."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.215,
            0.595,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "**Example 1 :** Given tan $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 4 } { 3 } }$ , find the other trigonometric ratios of the angle A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.285,
            0.594,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let us first draw a right   ABC (see Fig 8.8)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.331,
            0.465,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": "Now, we know that tan $\\mathrm{A}=\\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\mathrm{AB}}=\\frac{4}{3}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.38,
            0.595,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, if $\\mathbf { B } \\mathbf { C } = 4 k ,$ then $\\mathrm { A B } = 3 k$ , where k is a positive number."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.643,
            0.204,
            0.883,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.708,
                0.413,
                0.795,
                0.432
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.8"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.425,
            0.573,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "Now, by using the Pythagoras Theorem, we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.334,
            0.45,
            0.738,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "AC^{2} = AB^{2} + BC^{2} = (4k)^{2} + (3k)^{2} = 25k^{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.477,
            0.135,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.343,
            0.476,
            0.439,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { A C } = 5 k",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.502,
            0.75,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "Now, we can write all the trigonometric ratios using their definitions."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.327,
            0.527,
            0.555,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC} = \\frac{4k}{5k} = \\frac{4}{5}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.574,
            0.551,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "\\cos A = \\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{3k}{5k} = \\frac{3}{5}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.624,
            0.845,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, cot $\\mathrm{A} = \\frac{1}{\\tan \\mathrm{A}} = \\frac{3}{4},$ , cosec $\\mathrm{A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin \\mathrm{A}} = \\frac{5}{4}$ and sec $\\mathrm{A} = \\frac{1}{\\cos \\mathrm{A}} = \\frac{5}{3}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.687,
            0.455,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2 :** If $\\angle  B and  \\angle  Q$ are acute angles such that sin $\\mathbf { B } = \\sin \\mathbf { Q } ,$ then prove that $\\angle B = \\angle Q$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.759,
            0.455,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Let us consider two right triangles ABC and PQR where sin B = sin Q (see Fig. 8.9)."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.467,
            0.672,
            0.896,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.641,
                0.825,
                0.727,
                0.844
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.9"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.842,
            0.191,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "We have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.832,
            0.537,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": "\\sin \\mathbf { B } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { A C } } { \\mathrm { A B } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.887,
            0.142,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": "and"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.875,
            0.536,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": "\\sin Q = \\frac{PR}{PQ}",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
